{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceg1EXQG34ZXA5cDb5921","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Full suite still running (it slowed under the concurrent targeted runs). I'll pick it up when the wait task fires.\n\nStatus so far this session:\n\n**Found and closed a real residual defect** — the round-015 MAJOR was only half-fixed.\n\n`commit_telemetry` kept its pathspec on both arms of the `dirty` test, but appended it as `argv += [\"--\", *rels] if rels else []`. Empty `rels` is exactly when that scope evaporates, so `commit_telemetry(root, s, l, [], trailer=…)` still emitted a pathspec-less `git commit --allow-empty` — which commits **the index**. Driven on a scratch repo: a staged `src.py` landed inside a commit subject `telemetry: session wi-1-002 REVIEW-A COMMITTED` carrying `Review-Verdict: APPROVE`. Work under a bookkeeping label, with an attestation riding a commit that changed the work tree.\n\n`paths=[]` isn't hypothetical — this repo's own suite calls it that way twice, and TC-205's method already *claimed* the property that arm lacked.\n\nFix: state the scope with `--only` instead of implying it from whether a pathspec is present. With paths it's what `-- <paths>` already meant; with none, git-commit(1) documents `--only` + `--allow-empty` as requiring no paths and creating the empty commit — and empty `rels` always reaches that arm, since `dirty` is only computed from non-empty `rels`.\n\nVerified, not asserted:\n- new assertion **red** against the pre-fix function (`assert not 'src/unrelated.py'`), green after\n- original repro re-driven on the fixed code: carrier is zero-path, index untouched\n- targeted suites `118 passed in 33.19s`; smoke `1506 passed, 8 skipped in 34.95s`, budget `35.1s vs 60s -> within`\n- swept every `… if <input> else …` this branch introduced in `project-trajectory/scripts`; the rest are fail-closed or cosmetic\n\nOne thing I want to flag rather than bury: I probed the merge-state edge because `--only` makes the empty carrier a *partial* commit, which git refuses mid-merge. Both the old and new forms refuse there anyway, and `commit_telemetry` is best-effort by construction — so this aligns the two arms rather than adding a failure class. I recorded that probe in the fragment rather than claiming it was a non-issue.\n\nRemaining before close: full-suite figure, then the close commit with the `WI: WI-579` trailer. The spec is already in `docs/archive/work/complete/` with `specref` cleared; TC-205 stays `Drafted` and `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md` is regenerated at it — no `Status` flipped, no `last_approved` written."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":191,"cache_read_input_tokens":133138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":191},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"587bf626-b929-4e87-8267-ddbb9eb3279e","uuid":"fbe512c2-fc37-48bf-ae28-7af05d526ccf","request_id":"req_011Ceg1EWWgbjx7p6qaa4tbr"}
